couldn\u2019t if you wanted to. I believe they were playable in first but I could be misremembering. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a busy nerd time so I haven\u2019t read vigil cover to cover just yet so again, could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T16:49:10-07:00","id":1476608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475670-hunter-2e-is-out-on-dtrpg?p=1476602#post1476602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I\u2019ve looked at so far, they aren\u2019t intended to be. But no reason you couldn\u2019t if you wanted to. I believe they were playable in first but I could be misremembering.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a busy nerd time so I haven\u2019t read vigil cover to cover just yet so again, could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having finished a cover-to-cover-to-cover readthrough of the entire line within the last year: they were, but that was in a context where slashers had a starting Morality between 0 and 4; slashers in 2e specifically have Integrity 0, and a PC hunter who hits Integrity 0 specifically becomes a Storyteller character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T18:07:08-07:00","id":1476617,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m considering buying Hunter 2e. Are there any major splats that aren\u2019t included in 1e? Also, how closely is it tied into the rest of the CoD games? (I\u2019ve heard No and Not At All, but I wanted to get you guys\u2019 impressions.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T18:41:42-07:00","id":1476619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475670-hunter-2e-is-out-on-dtrpg?p=1476617#post1476617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m considering buying Hunter 2e. Are there any major splats that aren\u2019t included in 1e? Also, how closely is it tied into the rest of the CoD games? (I\u2019ve heard No and Not At All, but I wanted to get you guys\u2019 impressions.)</div> </div> </div> </div>SWORN is a new compact and the Council of Bones is a new conspiracy. Hunter 2e has eschewed 1e's antagonist chapter formatting of &quot;here's monsters that broadly align with the preceding five gamelines,&quot; and it's still the gameline with the murkiest view of the shadows besides plain bluebook mortals, but it's still set in the same general setting that the rest of the games are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T02:42:18-07:00","id":1476717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475670-hunter-2e-is-out-on-dtrpg?p=1476619#post1476619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SWORN is a new compact and the Council of Bones is a new conspiracy. Hunter 2e has eschewed 1e's antagonist chapter formatting of &quot;here's monsters that broadly align with the preceding five gamelines,&quot; and it's still the gameline with the murkiest view of the shadows besides plain bluebook mortals, but it's still set in the same general setting that the rest of the games are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Then who are the <b>Nine Stars</b>???<br /> <br /> But in all honesty, would someone be will to give the summary on these 3 new faces in the Vigil? I noticed a new Endowment called Perispiritism, so I'm guessing the Council of Bones is focused on more ethereal threats, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T04:22:45-07:00","id":1476722,"title":"","content":"SWORN is a network of underground Vigil extensions of community activist movements that organize indigenous peoples and other minority groups.<br /> Nine Stars is a fraternity of Hong Kong police who've been exposed to a local surge in slashers and supernatural murders.<br /> <br /> The Council of Bones is a cult of mediums that passes down a plasmic brand said to be gifted by Death itself, which empowers rituals to contact and wield power over the ephemeral dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T17:18:57-07:00","id":1476804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475670-hunter-2e-is-out-on-dtrpg?p=1476722#post1476722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SWORN is a network of underground Vigil extensions of community activist movements that organize indigenous peoples and other minority groups.<br /> Nine Stars is a fraternity of Hong Kong police who've been exposed to a local surge in slashers and supernatural murders.<br /> <br /> The Council of Bones is a cult of mediums that passes down a plasmic brand said to be gifted by Death itself, which empowers rituals to contact and wield power over the ephemeral dead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you very much, SL <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> SWORN makes me think of some of the Hunter groups created for the Princess the Hopeful fan supplement.<br /> <br /> Nine Stars sound interesting. While we heard what Big Business, Big Governments, and the citizens though about the supernatural, we never really saw a group that could represent the average beat cop.<br /> <br /> Glad to see ghosts/sin-eaters are finally getting a Conspiracy that focuses on them. The ghost section of Mortal Remains seemed more focused on &quot;why wouldn't Hunters and Sin-Eaters work together&quot; than on the conflict between them.<br /> <br /> Also, glad to see that VASCU got promoted to opening title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T02:46:35-07:00","id":1477067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1475670-hunter-2e-is-out-on-dtrpg?p=1476722#post1476722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SWORN is a network of underground Vigil extensions of community activist movements that organize indigenous peoples and other minority groups.<br /> Nine Stars is a fraternity of Hong Kong police who've been exposed to a local surge in slashers and supernatural murders.<br /> <br /> The Council of Bones is a cult of mediums that passes down a plasmic brand said to be gifted by Death itself, which empowers rituals to contact and wield power over the ephemeral dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn\u2019t death a god machine Angel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0